#lang treason

;; Slides: "Demo: Services in a Macro Template" and "Services in Macro Templates"
;;
;; The let in m's template is missing its body. Autocomplete there offers the
;; pattern variable p, the macro-introduced x, and m from the definition site,
;; but not y: the template's let body is macro-introduced, so hygiene keeps the
;; use site's y out of scope. Go-to-definition and find-references work in the
;; template too. These template services come from expanding the use (m 2).

(define-syntax m
  (syntax-rules ()
    [(m p) (let ([x p]) )]))

(let ([y 1]) (m 2))
